# <%= className %> gRPC service

Location: `apps/<%= fileName %>`. NestJS microservice, `Transport.GRPC`.

## Layout

- `proto/<%= fileName %>.proto` — the wire contract. Package `<%= propertyName %>`, service `<%= className %>`.
- `src/main.ts` — bootstraps the gRPC microservice (`GRPC_URL` env, default `0.0.0.0:5000`).
- `src/app.controller.ts` — RPC handlers, one `@GrpcMethod('<%= className %>', '<Rpc>')` per proto `rpc`.
- `src/app.service.ts` — business logic the handlers call.
- `nest-cli.json` — copies `proto/**/*.proto` into `dist/` on build.

## Adding an RPC

1. Add the `rpc` plus its request/response `message`s to `proto/<%= fileName %>.proto`.
2. Add a matching handler in `src/app.controller.ts` decorated
   `@GrpcMethod('<%= className %>', '<RpcName>')`. The method name may be camelCase;
   the decorator's second arg must match the proto `rpc` name exactly.
3. Keep request/response shapes as plain interfaces that mirror the proto messages.

## Running

```bash
nx serve <%= fileName %>      # nest start --watch
nx build <%= fileName %>
nx test <%= fileName %>
```

Deps are not installed by the generator — run `npm install` in `apps/<%= fileName %>` first.
